# Bind Keys in C++

In a Pawn or Character class, you can set up input in `SetupPlayerInputComponent`:

```cpp
void AMyCharacter::SetupPlayerInputComponent(UInputComponent* PlayerInputComponent)
{
    Super::SetupPlayerInputComponent(PlayerInputComponent);
    PlayerInputComponent->BindAction("Jump", IE_Pressed, this, &AMyCharacter::Jump);
    PlayerInputComponent->BindAxis("MoveForward", this, &AMyCharacter::MoveForward);
}
```
You need to have **Input Actions** and **Axis Mappings** defined in Project Settings → Input (or using Enhanced Input system in UE5).

Then define the functions:
```cpp
void AMyCharacter::MoveForward(float Value)
{
    if (Controller && Value != 0.0f)
    {
        AddMovementInput(GetActorForwardVector(), Value);
    }
}
```

