## Raycasting in C++

To detect what's in front of the player:
```cpp
FHitResult Hit;
FVector Start = GetActorLocation();
FVector End = Start + GetActorForwardVector() * 1000.0f;
FCollisionQueryParams Params;
Params.AddIgnoredActor(this);
bool bHit = GetWorld()->LineTraceSingleByChannel(Hit, Start, End, ECC_Visibility, Params);
if (bHit)
{
    AActor* HitActor = Hit.GetActor();
    // Do something
}
```
* `LineTraceSingleByChannel` returns the first blocking hit.
* `LineTraceMulti` returns all overlapping objects.
* Channels: `ECC_Visibility`, `ECC_WorldStatic`, etc.

This is fundamental for interaction systems, weapon hits, and AI perception.
